  "details": "I had a UX flow with the Max Avatar Download size where I would show people's avatars then immediately put it back on the shield setting which would load the avatar and keep it loaded until the avatar is unloaded and will replace it with the fallback. This flow broke w/ the most recent betas.\n\nWhat I'm proposing is a way to basically mimic this flow as I liked being able to selectively show heavier avatars and keep them shown but have it default back to fallbacks afterwards without having to manually reset the user's avatar visibility.\n\nI guess the closest analog would be like how setting the mic volume on someone else resets upon joining/rejoining an instance. I would like to be able to do something similar with Avatars.",
